            tagline = "A neighbourhood cycling project finds a way to return misplaced items and teach road awareness responsibly.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "The Unclaimed Bell", listOf("Chidi noticed a small opportunity to improve the community cycling project. At first, the task seemed small enough to finish in an afternoon. Then the group discovered that several people depended on the result, so they decided to slow down and understand the situation before making promises.", "As the project developed, Chidi and the team kept returning to the bell and equipment register. They learned that good work depends on clear records, respectful questions, and decisions that can be explained.", "One person offered a confident explanation, while another remembered events differently. The group listened respectfully and compared the accounts with dated records, learning that confidence alone does not make a detail correct. The group wrote the lesson in its journal so the next volunteers would know why the decision mattered.")),
                StoryPart(2, "A Simple Idea", listOf("Chidi noticed a small opportunity to improve the community cycling project. The students divided the work into clear roles. They kept a written record of decisions, checked important details with an adult who understood the subject, and made sure no one was expected to handle a responsibility beyond their experience.", "As the project developed, Chidi and the team kept returning to the bell and equipment register. They learned that good work depends on clear records, respectful questions, and decisions that can be explained.", "The first trial exposed a weakness that nobody had noticed on paper. The team paused, explained what had happened, and asked their supervisor to help them choose a safe adjustment. The group wrote the lesson in its journal so the next volunteers would know why the decision mattered.")),
                StoryPart(3, "The Register Begins", listOf("Chidi noticed a small opportunity to improve the community cycling project. A first draft brought the idea into focus, but it also revealed missing information. Rather than fill the gaps with guesses, the team marked each question and asked the people who could answer it.", "As the project developed, Chidi and the team kept returning to the bell and equipment register. They learned that good work depends on clear records, respectful questions, and decisions that can be explained.", "A disagreement grew when two volunteers preferred different solutions. Their mentor asked each person to explain the reason behind the suggestion, and the team found a way to test the ideas fairly. The group wrote the lesson in its journal so the next volunteers would know why the decision mattered.")),
                StoryPart(4, "A Confusing Return", listOf("Chidi noticed a small opportunity to improve the community cycling project. One person offered a confident explanation, while another remembered events differently. The group listened respectfully and compared the accounts with dated records, learning that confidence alone does not make a detail correct.", "As the project developed, Chidi and the team kept returning to the bell and equipment register. They learned that good work depends on clear records, respectful questions, and decisions that can be explained.", "A neighbour contributed a useful memory, but asked the students not to publish their name. The team respected that request and recorded only the information they had permission to share. The group wrote the lesson in its journal so the next volunteers would know why the decision mattered.")),
